Data   : declared source useVehicles -> PeriodComparePageViewModel binds shared S8 VehiclesStore.vehicles()
         (web useVehicles ▸ GET /vehicles) via periodCompareSource(); fills the vehicle picker and drives the
         page-level loading/empty/error/success. The two-window comparison reads GET /analytics/period-stats
         (?vehicle_id&days) for Period A and Period B. That endpoint has NO KMP AnalyticsRepository/Store binding
         (the web page reads it with a raw request(), not a useXxx hook), so — mirroring the web verbatim — the
         page fetches it with the shared resilient ApiHttpClient.request<PeriodStats>() obtained from the process
         AuthContainer.apiHttpClient. The shared DataContainer/KMP core are NOT modified (no predecessor change,
         no new repository/contract/golden surface); only TeslaSyncApplication is touched for host registration.
SI/units: backend period-stats arrive in display units (total_distance km, energy_used kWh, avg_efficiency Wh/km,
         co2_saved kg). Distance is converted km -> SI metres -> the user's unit via convertDistanceFromSI; the
         Wh/km efficiency folds to Wh/mi for mile users; all at the model boundary (S5) bound to the live
         unitFormatter (web useUnits). Values stay SI on the wire; conversion is display-only.
Strings: 0 added — all 34 compare.* keys already exist in res/values/strings.xml (+ values-ar/values-he);
         web key names preserved (compare.* -> translation_compare_*; compare.banner.toFleetCta ->
